  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 2-Tridecanone and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately interact with this complex. Specifically, 2-Tridecanone is directly linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED/RBBP7/RBBP4 complex, which in turn is targeted by compounds such as 4-Nonene, Bisnorstriatol, and Chrysothol, all of which are known to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This indicates a possible pathway where 2-Tridecanone may influence the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through its interaction with these intermediate targets. The scores across all three paths are consistent, suggesting a strong and reliable relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible biological connection, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of 2-Tridecanone in the regulation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex.",
